WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.918 --> 00:00:04.421
We're in the Oprah slash 
Diane Sawyer...

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:07.174
you know, Barbara Walters

00:00:07.174 --> 00:00:08.508
-Warmth. 

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.801
Octavia.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.846
-Yes, Kate.
-Thank you for joining us today.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.305
[laughter]

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:15.349
♪♪

00:00:17.893 --> 00:00:18.936
So, here we are. 

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:21.355
[laughter]

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:22.981
You know what I was 
thinking about, was,

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:26.068
how excited I am to actually
promote the show.

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:27.110
-Yes.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.446
Because it's been so much
fun for us to work together.

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:32.658
Working with you is
one of the most amazing gifts.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:33.867
-Awww.
You know?

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:36.703
Oh, my god I mean...
I have separation anxiety.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.537
I do too.
[laughter]

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.040
I'm like, I'm going to start
crying right now.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.666
[laughter]

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:41.750
♪♪

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.127
Kate, let me just tell you honey

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:47.130
with how crazy T.V. 
schedules are...

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:51.009
you've got to be able to
count on your scene partners.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:55.180
And you're- you're more than
gifted actress, that we know.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.184
You just have this 
disarming calm.

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:02.396
Whenever we get the scene
up on its feet

00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:04.064
after you leave, it's like

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.941
ugh, wait is it just me by
myself now?

00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:07.818
[laughter]
-No! No!

00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:09.111
There's no fun there.

00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:11.113
We're real scene partners, 
it's true.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:15.701
In the show, it's a
complicated relationship.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:19.288
Poppy and Micah, we're friends
from when we were kids.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:22.291
We haven't seen each other
In a bit, and then, boom.

00:01:22.291 --> 00:01:24.084
We find my husband murdered.

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:26.837
These women, love each other 
so much and

00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:28.171
there's so much we're hiding.  

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:28.547
-Yep.

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:31.967
And we're constantly forcing
each other to open up.

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:34.428
I loved the first season,
but I feel like we really

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:35.929
went there with this season.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.556
It feels really personal.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.725
Poppy I need you to help me

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:41.310
find out what happened to Joshua.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.522
Seeking answers is never
a straight line.

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:47.649
♪♪

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:50.068
What's your favorite part
about this season?

00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:54.489
My favorite part about this
season is through Micah

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.451
and Poppy's relationship...
Poppy has to deal with

00:01:57.451 --> 00:02:01.121
her demons to solve 
Josh's murder.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:05.751
And I love that it's also from
the perspective of this

00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:07.711
life-long friendship.

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:12.758
I want to have the gravitas
of this character,

00:02:12.758 --> 00:02:15.635
but also have some of the humor
and the fun that we got to play.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.470
-Yeah.

00:02:17.721 --> 00:02:19.765
Why did you want to play Micah?

00:02:19.765 --> 00:02:22.392
Why did I want to do this show?
First of all, was-

00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:24.603
really because of you.
-Oh!

00:02:24.603 --> 00:02:27.064
Before I even really knew what
it was I like,

00:02:27.064 --> 00:02:28.607
This is gonna be really fun.

00:02:28.607 --> 00:02:31.902
I thought, what a great world
to enter into.

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:34.654
♪♪

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.157
I think, the thing is that's
so fun about doing something

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:40.744
like this is, that there's
intensity in terms of character

00:02:40.744 --> 00:02:42.829
dynamic and serious story lines.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.206
But at the end of the day

00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:45.791
this is a whodunnit?
-Yeah.

00:02:45.791 --> 00:02:48.085
And who's doing it?
And who did it?

00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:50.504
♪♪

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:53.340
There's something just juicy
and fun about it.

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:56.301
♪♪

00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:58.387
You're gonna try to figure out
who did it--

00:02:58.387 --> 00:02:59.888
-Yeah.
-like, on episode one.

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:01.181
-Yeah.
-And that's exciting for me.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.182
[Both] It's so fun.

00:03:02.516 --> 00:03:04.768
♪♪

00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:07.396
It's constantly keeping you
guessing.

00:03:07.396 --> 00:03:08.855
-Guessing.
And I love that.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.856
-Me too.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:16.655
♪♪

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:20.784
That was a love fest.

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:22.285
-That was a love fest and it--

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:23.537
-was effortless.
-I love it.

00:03:23.537 --> 00:03:26.498
That is a two thumbs up
for me.

00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:28.875
♪♪

